@startuml
' Pile Visibility Flow — Mutual Pile Visibility (intention #34)
' Shows the end-to-end flow: GameCore.get_state() → API → frontend pile viewer.

skinparam sequenceFontSize 11

title Pile Visibility — End-to-End Flow (intention #34)

actor User

box "Frontend" #LightYellow
    participant GameBoard
    participant App
    participant "api.js" as API
end box

box "Backend" #LightBlue
    participant "Controller\napi.py" as Controller
    participant GameCore
    participant PlayerState
end box

== Game State Request (always full piles) ==

User -> GameBoard : clicks pile count (P1 or P2)
GameBoard -> App : onViewPiles(pid)
App -> App : read state.players[pid].draw_pile\nand state.players[pid].discard_pile\ndirectly from state (no API call)

note right of App
  **Design/34 change**
  state already contains full
  piles for BOTH players.
  No perspective param needed.
  getMyPiles() API removed.
end note

App -> GameBoard : setPileViewer({ pid, draw_pile, discard_pile })
GameBoard -> User : show pile viewer modal\n"Your Piles" or "Opponent's Piles"

== Backend: get_state() always returns full piles ==

Controller -> GameCore : get_state()\n(player_perspective deprecated)
GameCore -> PlayerState : build PlayerState for P1
GameCore -> PlayerState : build PlayerState for P2

note right of PlayerState
  **Design/34 change**
  draw_pile: list[CardType] (always)
  discard_pile: list[CardType] (always)
  No more None values.
  No conditional branching.
end note

GameCore --> Controller : GameState with full piles for both
Controller --> API : {"players": {"1": {draw_pile:[...], discard_pile:[...]},\n"2": {draw_pile:[...], discard_pile:[...]}}}

== During Game Creation ==

User -> App : start game (PVP or PVE)
App -> API : createGame(mode, ai)
API -> Controller : POST /api/games
Controller -> GameCore : start_game()
Controller -> GameCore : get_state()
GameCore --> Controller : GameState (both piles visible)
Controller --> API : state with both players' piles
API --> App : state
App -> GameBoard : render status bar with\nclickable pile counts for both players

@enduml
